Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• products_23.applicant_full_name : filter for the company (‘SanofiAventis’).  
• products_23.product_id         : key that links products to formulations.  
• products_23.trade_name         : trade (brand) name to be returned.  
• products_23.approval_date      : decide which record is the most recent.  
• formulations_23.product_id     : join field coming from the product table.  
• formulations_23.molregno       : ChEMBL unique identifier for a molecule; what we finally want to de‑duplicate on.

Principal conditions we will need  
1. WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'                -- exact match as requested  
2. JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23` f  
   ON  p.product_id = f.product_id                             -- link product ↔ formulation  
3. GROUP BY or window functions on molregno                    -- keep only latest approval_date

Below are ten different exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows).  
Use whichever fits best in your own analysis environment.

```sql
-- 1) Quick look at the first 20 rows of the ChEMBL‑23 products table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) List distinct company (applicant) names – alphabetically, first 20
SELECT DISTINCT applicant_full_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
ORDER BY applicant_full_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) What do Sanofi‑related spellings look like? (case–insensitive)
SELECT DISTINCT applicant_full_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE LOWER(applicant_full_name) LIKE '%sanofi%'
ORDER BY applicant_full_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Check if an exact literal match “SanofiAventis” exists
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Retrieve product id, trade name, approval date for that exact company
SELECT product_id,
       trade_name,
       approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`
WHERE applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Join products to formulations to see which molecules (molregno) show up
SELECT f.molregno,
       p.product_id,
       p.trade_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`      AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23`  AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Molecule, trade name, and approval date together
SELECT f.molregno,
       p.trade_name,
       p.approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`      AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23`  AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Latest approval date per molecule (simple GROUP BY + MAX)
SELECT f.molregno,
       MAX(p.approval_date) AS latest_approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`      AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23`  AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
GROUP BY f.molregno
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as #8 but also show *one* representative trade name for each molecule
SELECT f.molregno,
       ANY_VALUE(p.trade_name)        AS trade_name,
       MAX(p.approval_date)           AS latest_approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`      AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23`  AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
GROUP BY f.molregno
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final pattern: keep only the rows that are the most recent per molecule
SELECT DISTINCT
       f.molregno,
       p.trade_name,
       MAX(p.approval_date) OVER (PARTITION BY f.molregno) AS latest_approval_date
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.products_23`      AS p
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.ebi_chembl.formulations_23`  AS f
  ON p.product_id = f.product_id
WHERE p.applicant_full_name = 'SanofiAventis'
QUALIFY p.approval_date = MAX(p.approval_date) OVER (PARTITION BY f.molregno)
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is limited to 20 rows so you can inspect intermediate results safely before moving on to larger extractions.
